    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/9ncuT5DP#mOYZ6CRi",
      "title": "A private child, composed once",
      "narrative": "The workbench proves the executable and prepares an Archboard-only Codex home that every Archboard server on the machine shares, so one sign-in serves them all; it fills in the auto-review defaults its config.toml lacks and keeps what Codex or a person set. The owner lock and epoch ledger are the server's own. Then it starts the child and builds one generation's parts in the order they depend on each other.",
