    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/9ncuT5DP#9Ee1KNBg",
      "title": "A tab holds one coordinator and a workhorse for each checkout",
      "narrative": "Each browser tab is a tab session with its own lease and its own coordinator. A pane's first message or Talk starts its conversation: the coordinator first, then the workhorse of the checkout that pane shows, which that checkout's link then names. The pane that holds the lease sends its typed message straight to that workhorse as a turn or a steer, and edits that thread's queue. A pane that moves to another checkout reaches the workhorse there instead. The coordinator's work goes through the four operations, each staged in the epoch ledger so a child that dies mid-flight leaves a stated outcome rather than a guess.",
