    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/9ncuT5DP#ISHYhZ6k",
      "title": "Voice is a separate thread that works in no checkout",
      "narrative": "Each tab session has its own coordinator, a thread with its own model and settings, started with the tab's first message or Talk. It runs in a directory of its own that holds no vault, so every command it runs names its checkout with -C. It is the voice model's subconscious: it reads the boards, follows the workhorses and decides what the voice model says, and it runs only while voice is live. It does bounded work itself and routes anything sustained to the workhorse of the checkout it names, starting that workhorse when there is none. Two tabs can talk at the same time, each to its own coordinator.",
