      "id": "vKEsyHFk/9ncuT5DP#XARzanTh",
      "title": "A tab session ends 60 seconds after its last pane closes",
      "narrative": "Every pane names its tab when its socket opens. When no pane of the tab comes back for 60 seconds, the session ends: its lease and link go, its pending approvals are cancelled, voice and board news stop, and each of its threads is unsubscribed once no turn runs on it, so Codex unloads it. A reload within that time keeps the conversation and its approvals. When the child exits, every session is dropped, and a tab's next message starts a new workhorse.",
